# Preferred short project codes appended to CCD session titles, so a title reads
# "Rename Sessions - D" and the sidebar shows which repo a session belongs to.
# Read by ~/.claude/hooks/session-title.sh; conventions documented in
# ~/.claude/skills/session-title/SKILL.md.
#
# A repo absent from this list still gets a code — the hook guesses one from the
# initials of the hyphen-separated words (mock-controller → MC, platform → P),
# capped at three characters. This file overrides that guess.
#
# So a row is worth adding when the guess would be wrong, too long, or would
# collide with a code already in use. Every row below happens to match what the
# guess produces anyway; they're here to reserve those codes, so a later
# mock-dashboard gets pinned to something else instead of quietly becoming a
# second MD. Keep codes unique — nothing enforces it.
#
# <repo name>     <CODE>
platform          P
mock-controller   MC
mock-dock         MD
drone-userland    DU
infrastructure    I
dotfiles          D
omnibus		  O
